  "solutions": [
    {
      "source_number": "161",
      "independent_solution": "Over real numbers: a) x=2y gives 7y^2=20, hence (x,y)=(2t,t), t=+-sqrt(20/7); x=-2y gives y^2=20, hence (-2t,t), t=+-2sqrt(5). b) x=3y/2 gives -y^2/4=-1, hence (3,2),(-3,-2); x=-3y/2 gives 11y^2/4=-1 and no real solutions. c) p=xy satisfies p^2+p-72=(p-8)(p+9)=0; s=x+y=6. For p=8: (2,4),(4,2); p=-9: (3+3sqrt(2),3-3sqrt(2)) and its swap. d) s^2-2s-15=0 gives s=5 or -3, p=11-s. s=5,p=6 yields (2,3),(3,2); s=-3,p=14 has discriminant -47, no real solutions."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "162",
      "independent_solution": "a) Write numerator n and denominator d with all denominators nonzero. (n+2)/(d+3)=n/d implies 3n=2d, so the original value is 2/3. The second relation gives (n+1)/(d+6)=1/2; substituting n=2d/3 yields d=12,n=8, original fraction 8/12. b) d=2n-1 from (n+1)/(d+3)=1/2. The product condition is 5n(n-1)=d(d+1)=2n(2n-1), hence n(n-3)=0. n=0,d=-1 makes d+1=0 and is inadmissible; n=3,d=5 gives 3/5."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "163",
      "independent_solution": "a) Positive sides a,b satisfy a^2+b^2=289,ab=120, so (a+b)^2=529 and a+b=23. Roots of z^2-23z+120 are 8,15 dm. b) Legs a,b satisfy a^2+b^2=676,ab=240, giving a+b=sqrt(1156)=34; legs 10,24 cm and perimeter 10+24+26=60 cm."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "164",
      "independent_solution": "a) a^2+b^2=169 and (a+3)^2+(b+3)^2=289 imply 6(a+b)+18=120, so a+b=17 and ab=60; legs 5,12 m. Area increase [3(a+b)+9]/2=30 m^2. b) Small legs a,b satisfy a^2+b^2=25; adding 17 to each gives hypotenuse 29, so 34(a+b)+578=816 and a+b=7,ab=12, legs 3,4 dm. Large legs 20,21 dm. Area increase [17(a+b)+289]/2=204 dm^2."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "165",
      "independent_solution": "a) Let u,v be full-pool hours of first and second pipes. 1/u+1/v=1/40 and u/3+2v/3=78 imply uv=40(u+v),u+2v=234. Thus 2v^2-274v+9360=0; v=65 or 72, with u=104 or 90 respectively. Both positive ordered pairs (104,65),(90,72) satisfy both conditions. b) Full-field hours u,v satisfy uv=20(u+v) and v/3=u/2-3. Substitute v=3u/2-9: 3u^2-118u+360=0. u=36,v=45 are positive; u=10/3,v=-4 inadmissible. Answer first 36, second 45 h."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "166",
      "independent_solution": "a) Let first speed u, second speed v, first premeeting hours t; second premeeting t-1. Second premeeting distance is 2.5u, first is 2.5u+2, so t=2.5+2/u. After meeting first takes 2.5 h and second takes 2.4 h (arrival 0.1 h earlier), hence 2.4v=2.5u+2. Also v(t-1)=2.5u. Elimination gives 9u^2-32u-16=0, u=4 or -4/9. Positive solution u=4,v=5 km/h, total distance 5u+2=22 km. b) Bus premeeting time t, motorcycle t-0.5. Motorcycle postmeeting 1 h, bus 1.5 h. ut=v, v(t-0.5)=1.5u; t(t-0.5)=1.5 gives t=1.5 (negative root rejected). v=1.5u,90=u(1.5+1.5), so bus 30, motorcycle 45 km/h."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "167",
      "independent_solution": "a) Meeting time 56/60=14/15 h, hence u+v=120. Train from A arrives 1/4 h earlier: 112/v-112/u=1/4. Positive solution u=64,v=56 km/h. b) Let meeting time t, speeds u from A and v from B. vt=u/3 and ut=3v/4; t^2=1/4, so t=1/2 h, u/v=3/2. Since (u+v)t=80, u=96,v=64 km/h."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "168",
      "independent_solution": "a) Expansion coefficients are a,ab+1,b+4a-3,4-3b,-12. Equating gives ab=-10,b=3-4a,c=4-3b. 4a^2-3a-10=0 yields (a,b,c)=(2,-5,19),(-5/4,8,-20); both leading coefficients nonzero. b) Coefficients are 3,-11,c+6+3q,-3c-2q,qc. Thus -3c-2q=0,qc=-24, n=c+6+3q. c=4,q=-6,n=-8 or c=-4,q=6,n=20."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "169",
      "independent_solution": "a) Base b, equal side l, rhombus side r=24. Similarity gives r/b+r/l=1 (opposite rhombus vertex on the other triangle side), so bl=24(b+l). Together b+2l=140 gives l^2-82l+1680=0, l=40 or 42. Valid triangle sides (40,40,60),(42,42,56) dm. b) Rectangle height h gives width w=120(1-h/60)=120-2h. wh=1750 implies h=25 or 35; corresponding w=70 or 50, perimeter 190 or 170 cm. Both fit within height 60."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "170",
      "independent_solution": "All six include equality boundaries. a) Closed halfplane y>=x/3-4/3. b) Closed halfplane y<=x-1/2. c) At/above upward V y=|x|, vertex (0,0). d) At/below downward V y=-|x|. e) At/above V y=|x-2|, vertex (2,0). f) At/below V y=|1-x|=|x-1|, vertex (1,0)."
