      "independent_solution": "a) Any entire straight line in y>3 must be horizontal y=c with c>3; a nonhorizontal line has y unbounded below. Example y=4. b) For a vertical quadratic parabola y=ax^2+bx+c entirely in y>5, necessary and sufficient a>0 and vertex minimum c-b^2/(4a)>5. Example y=x^2+6. y=x^2+5 touches the excluded boundary; downward or sideways parabolas are not wholly above 5."
